{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftML"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Early Stopping & Generalization Control"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/SupervisedClassifiers","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/SupervisedRegressors","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/PreparedRegression","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/PreparedClassification","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/CoreMLInference","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/BoundedInference","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EnsembleLearning","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/HistogramGradientBoosting","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/ReproducibilityAndPRNG","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/MLOpsExport","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/ReusableCPUPrediction"],"generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterative estimators like multi-layer perceptrons (","type":"text"},{"code":"MLPClassifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"MLPRegressor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and gradient boosted decision trees (","type":"text"},{"code":"GradientBoostedTreesRegressor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") improve their training loss over successive iterations. However, after sufficient capacity has been fit, additional epochs frequently lead to overfitting on training noise and deteriorating generalization on unseen data.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"EarlyStopping","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides a decoupled, value-type training callback that monitors validation loss or performance metrics across successive epochs, halting training and optionally r